.TH GIT-ROOST 1 "2026-07-31" "git-roost 0.9.1" "User Commands" \" x-release-please-version
.SH NAME
git\-roost \- top for git, across every repo and worktree on the box
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B git\-roost
.RI [ options ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B git\-roost
shows every git working tree it can find in one table, grouped by what it costs
to ignore: trees stuck part\-way through a rebase or merge first, then diverged
trees, then uncommitted work, then unpushed commits, then trees that have fallen
behind.
.PP
It is a companion to
.BR roost (1),
which reports on Claude Code sessions. Sessions report what they intend to do;
git reports what actually happened.
.PP
.B git\-roost
is read\-only by construction: every git invocation is checked against an
allowlist of read\-only plumbing and raises otherwise, so the tool cannot modify
a working tree, an index or a ref. The allowlist is keyed on the subcommand and
its first argument together, since
.B stash list
and
.B stash pop
are not the same kind of operation.
.PP
A bare run opens the TUI and scans the current directory. Override with
.B \-\-root
or
.BR $GIT_ROOST_ROOT .
A configured root that does not exist (or is not a directory) is an error.
If the root exists but no repositories are found within
.BR \-\-depth ,
the table is replaced by the paths that were searched and the
.B \-\-root
invocation that would scan somewhere else. Use
.B \-\-once
(or pipe stdout) for a one\-shot table instead of the TUI.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BR \-w ", " \-\-watch " [\fISECS\fR]"
Redraw every \fISECS\fR seconds, default 3. This is the default mode on a
TTY. It is a viewport the size of the terminal, not a scrolling dump: the
status line stays on screen and
\fBj\fR/\fBk\fR move a row cursor through trees that do not fit.
.TP
.BR \-\-log " [\fIN\fR]"
Show a commit feed merged across every repository, newest first, default 25
entries. Commits are deduplicated per repository, so a repo and its worktrees do
not each contribute a copy.
.TP
.BR \-1 ", " \-\-once
Render once and exit. Overrides \fB\-\-watch\fR. Also used automatically when
stdout is not a TTY (pipes and redirects).
.TP
.BR \-a ", " \-\-all
Expand the collapsed QUIET group.
.TP
.BR \-\-root " \fIDIR\fR"
Where to look for repositories. Repeatable. Default is
.BR $GIT_ROOST_ROOT
if set, otherwise the current directory. A root that does not exist or is not
a directory exits with status 1.
.TP
.BR \-\-depth " \fIN\fR"
How deep to search below each root, default 3. Worktrees kept beside a repo live
at <root>/.worktrees/<repo>/<slug>, which is depth 3.
.TP
.B \-\-json
Emit the collected records as JSON rather than a table.
.TP
.B \-\-no\-color
Disable colour output.
.TP
.B \-\-ascii
Keep the ASCII glyph dialect in watch mode. Without it, watch mode uses the
Unicode dialect (\fB\(ua2\fR/\fB\(da3\fR arrows for DRIFT, check marks
for CI, framed overlays) when stdout is an interactive UTF\-8 terminal \(em on
Windows, only under Windows Terminal (\fBWT_SESSION\fR set), since a legacy
console reports UTF\-8 but cannot draw the glyphs. Pipe\-safe output
(\fB\-\-once\fR, \fB\-\-json\fR, \fB\-\-check\fR, anything redirected) is
always ASCII and needs no flag. Same as setting \fBGIT_ROOST_ASCII\fR.
.TP
.B \-\-check
Print nothing but a summary and exit 1 if any tree is mid\-operation,
diverged or has uncommitted work; 0 otherwise. For scripts and hooks, not the
table. Always one\-shot, always ASCII.
.TP
.B \-\-github
Add a PR/CI column via
.BR gh (1).
Opt\-in: network calls; needs \fBgh\fR on PATH and authenticated, silently
omitted otherwise.
.TP
.BR \-\-print\-completion " \fISHELL\fR"
Print a completion script for \fISHELL\fR (bash, zsh or powershell) to
standard output and exit. Eval or source it from the shell's profile.
.TP
.B \-\-version
Print the version and exit.
.SH COLUMNS
.TP
.B WORK
Uncommitted work: \fBclean\fR, a count of tracked changes, \fB+N?\fR untracked,
or both. Untracked files are marked but never promoted to the UNCOMMITTED group.
.TP
.B DRIFT
Position against the base branch: \fB=\fR in sync, \fB^N\fR ahead, \fBvN\fR
behind, \fB^NvM\fR diverged, \fB\-\fR unknown. A dash means unknown, never in
sync. In the Unicode dialect (watch mode on a capable terminal, see
\fB\-\-ascii\fR) the same cell is drawn with up and down arrows: U+2191 N
ahead, U+2193 N behind.
.IP
The baseline is the branch's upstream if it has one, else \fBorigin/HEAD\fR,
else \(em when the repository has exactly one remote \(em that remote's
\fBHEAD\fR, \fBmain\fR or \fBmaster\fR. With two or more remotes and no
\fBorigin/HEAD\fR the baseline is reported as unknown rather than guessed.
.TP
.B STASH
Number of stash entries, blank when there are none.
.TP
.B LAST
Age of the most recent commit.
.TP
.B PR
Only with \fB\-\-github\fR. \fB#123\fR open, \fB#123+\fR CI green,
\fB#123x\fR CI red, \fB#123~\fR CI still running, \fB#123 draft\fR, blank when
there is no open PR. In the Unicode dialect the CI marks are U+2713 (check),
U+2717 (cross) and U+25CB (circle) in place of \fB+\fR, \fBx\fR and \fB~\fR.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B GIT_ROOST_ROOT
Directories to search, separated like
.B PATH
(colon on Unix, semicolon on Windows). When unset, git-roost uses the usual
checkout folders under the home directory that exist, else the current
directory.
.B \-\-root
overrides this for one invocation.
.TP
.B GIT_ROOST_WORKERS
Size of the thread pool used to scan trees. Default 12.
.TP
.B GIT_ROOST_TIMEOUT
Seconds before an individual git call is abandoned. Default 5.
.TP
.B GIT_ROOST_ASCII
If set to any value, watch mode keeps the ASCII glyph dialect; same as
\fB\-\-ascii\fR. Pipe\-safe output is ASCII regardless.
.TP
.B WT_SESSION
Set by Windows Terminal, not by git\-roost. On Windows it is what admits the
Unicode dialect: a legacy console reports UTF\-8 too but cannot draw it.
.TP
.B NO_COLOR
If set, colour output is disabled. See https://no-color.org.
.SH EXIT STATUS
Returns 0 on success, including when no repositories are found.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR roost (1),
.BR git\-status (1),
.BR git\-worktree (1)
.SH AUTHOR
George M. Howard <dev@swamplink.com>
